# Apply an implemented y-menu verb to a target that cannot respond, and let the
# screen say whether the game told the player anything. Read by
# tools/check_yuse_no_effect.sh, bd inc-k8uw.
#
# Pour is implemented (src/Tables.cpp:3335) but has no handler for an ordinary
# item: the one EV_POUR script in the tree refills a brass lantern from a flask
# of oil (lib/mundane.irh:640) and returns NOTHING for anything else without
# printing. Player::YuseMenu threw the event and read nothing back, so the
# player saw no line at all. Two dumps pin the run: pour-target proves the
# target prompt was reached, after-pour is the screen the check reads.

@include chargen.keys

y
@choose "Pour"
@choose "loincloth"
@dump:pour-target
@choose "orcish longspear"
@dump:after-pour
@quit
